+// ── G7 · one base, and WCAG 2.5.3 under EVERY arm ──────────────────────────────────────────
+// The written glyph must be a substring of the name (label-in-name), read per `SIX_ARM`: arm (a)
+// and (b) write the count, arm (c) writes the remainder after five strokes and names itself
+// `6 players, 5 plus 1`. Pass 5 wrote "(c) would pass" and (c) failed at N = 6/9/14/15/16; pass 6
+// named it `5 players and 1 more`, which borrowed the sheet's `and N more` for a second referent.
+// The widths are printed per N: arm (c)'s head grows with its digits (row 4 of the ballot).
