+// ── PRM engaged MID-DRAW: the stroke lands inked and stays inked (pass-4 critic §2.4) ──────
+// `settle()` is what the reduced-motion watch calls; a stroke caught mid-draw must read 0 on the
+// frames after the switch and never rise again. The row samples the newcomer's dash every frame.
+// Pass 4's per-key `stop()` inside `settle()` had no gate; ablated here it stayed green in both
+// engines (the chain has already force-cleared the tween), so pass 5 struck it. What this row
+// holds is the watch: strike `watch(reducedMotion, …)` and the stroke strands mid-reveal, RED.
+test("reduced motion engaged mid-draw lands the stroke inked, and it stays inked", async ({
+  page,
